{"id":"af7b5bf9-9ebb-47f0-9bc4-dcfbaba8b690","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1dd11584a6dd6476","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-problems.ts","baseline":{"blob":"165a03cd4e0af6883e8fde079006523da6d10c2e","start":0,"end":67},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","GitFileChange","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/git","\""]},"context":{"after":"a4eb2d27eddc588a"}},"payload":{"text":"A change's problems, against HEAD: `code.problems` { paths?, depth?, limit? } answers which diagnostics the working\ntree's changes added and which they cleared, so a person or an agent can tell what a change broke from the problems\nthat were there before it (a whole program's TypeScript errors hide the new ones). Its readers: the review panel\n(shell/change-problems.tsx, each changed file's) and agents' `code_problems`.\n\n- TypeScript's, from the change-problems extension's tsserver plugin (`_changeProblems.compare`,\nextensions/change-problems/ts-plugin.js): the changed files and the files importing them, each checked as the program\nis now and as it was at HEAD. The projects are told of the files made since first (`_changeProblems.files`), and each\nchanged file's symbols are asked, so the server holds its project.\n- ESLint's, per changed file (`_eslint.problems`, the eslint extension): its HEAD text and its text now, each linted at\nits path, customized as the Problems view's are.\n\nA problem is the same one at HEAD and now when its file, source, code and message are: lines move with an edit, so\nwhere it is doesn't say. Now is what the editor has (an open file's unsaved edits included); HEAD is git's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:10.421Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:17:10.421Z"}
{"id":"d3dfcc28-af5f-4f83-bd86-7216edf272bf","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"fe1aeaf592e96bf7","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-problems.ts","baseline":{"blob":"ec58b64b6ea849b7e2c51ad2a69ec7218ab8dca4","start":4483,"end":4747},"shape":{"type":"For","atoms":["for","(","let","tried","=","1",";","heads",".","size",">","0","&&","tried","<","TRIES","&&","(","compared","===","undefined","||","(","compared",".","error","===","undefined","&&","compared",".","projects",".","length","===","0",")",")",";","tried","+=","1",")","{","await","new","Promise","(","(","resolve",")","=>","{","setTimeout","(","resolve",",","TRY_MS",")",";","}",")",";","compared","=","await","ask","(",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"6f455b8da751a821","after":"bf2c36cd58ce0705#0"}},"payload":{"text":"A server just started doesn't know the request until it makes a project (the plugin registers it then), and holds\nno project for a file it's still opening: it's asked again, a little later.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:16:48.122Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:16:48.122Z"}
{"id":"d8f525ef-452e-4286-b06f-b086886fdc2e","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0e39f35c1636c57e#1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/code-problems.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a97e451c7d58e9c6250bf59fc6fdf4937a2026a1","start":9801,"end":9812},"shape":{"type":"String","atoms":["\"","unchecked","\""]},"context":{"before":"d7c25d57a05140c8","after":"800887f0319ad63e"}},"payload":{"text":"What it didn't look at, so an empty `added` isn't read as more than it is.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:16:10.045Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:16:10.045Z"}
